I use the "cmd" command, then "mode con lines=100", then "nethack -s100".

"mode con lines=25" is also useful if the command-line window defaults to 
50 lines per screen. (I hate looking at that.)

Just for the heck of it, here are my nethack and slashem batch files:

[nh.bat]:
mode con lines=25
c:
cd\nethack
nethack
hearse

[sl.bat]
mode con lines=25
c:
cd\slashemd
slashem
hearse

I could make batch files for the score lists, I guess...

But I "grew up" on the MS-DOS command line, and it does my heart good to 
see that "C:\>" once in a while.

